# fonts-jamos: the fonts and the fontconfig configuration of Jam OS (G2's
# GP2, docs/G2-PLAN.md section 4), a data port (style data: files and no
# build). Chromium builds its own fontconfig, FreeType and HarfBuzz; what it
# needs from the system is font files and a fonts.conf, and the shell sets
# FONTCONFIG_FILE to /pkg/share/fonts/fonts.conf for every program.
#
# The set: Liberation Sans, Serif and Mono (metric-compatible with Arial,
# Times New Roman and Courier New), Noto Sans, Serif and Sans Mono (Latin,
# Greek and Cyrillic: the upstream "latin-greek-cyrillic" releases, the
# static unhinted TrueType files; FreeType's own hinting does the rest),
# Inter (the static files of its nine weights and their italics; not the
# Display cut, and not the variable files, whose family is "Inter Variable"),
# JetBrains Mono (all its
# static TrueType files) and Noto Color Emoji (the bitmap, CBDT, font that
# Chromium's FreeType draws). CJK later, as a package of its own.
#
# Every font here is under the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Each licence text
# is a file of its own in the package (share/licences/fonts-jamos/), taken
# from the same upstream release as the fonts and given a distinct name:
# several archives carry an OFL.txt of their own, and each would overwrite
# the last when unpacked together.
